Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-29-2000||07:03 PM||||Sounds like she is talking about the early Chevy 2.8L.  This engine was never put in a Feiro from the factory.  The easy way would be to prove what was in ther car in the first place.  There are also numbers on the engines and tranies that are traceable to the build numbers in your VIN I think.  If the engine from your car was not original, then you might be screwed.  <P>~$500 for CV's and a motor... you could have gotten a much better deal at a mechanic!<P>good Luck,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
